                     <h2 data-scramble data-i18n="about_heading">From raw data<br>to <em>something useful</em></h2>
                     <div class="about-body">
                         <p data-i18n="about_p1">I'm a London-based Data Scientist and Python Developer, trained at Imperial College London (96% average). My day-to-day spans the whole data workflow: cleaning messy datasets, building and tuning models, and shipping the result as something people can actually use, not just a notebook that lives on my laptop.</p>
-                        <p data-i18n="about_p2">Outside client and product work, I build my own things: Android apps, trading tools, generative art systems, live wallpapers, screensavers, word-cloud typography. Forty-six projects so far, spread across the <strong>Google Play Store</strong>, <strong>Gumroad</strong>, <strong>Envato</strong>, and <strong>Lemon Squeezy</strong>. Running these myself taught me things a job rarely does: how to price something, when to ship versus keep polishing, and what users actually respond to once a product is out in the world.</p>
+                        <p data-i18n="about_p2">Outside client and product work, I build my own things: Android apps, trading tools, generative art systems, live wallpapers, screensavers, word-cloud typography. Fifty-plus projects so far, spread across the <strong>Google Play Store</strong>, <strong>Gumroad</strong>, <strong>Envato</strong>, and <strong>Lemon Squeezy</strong>. Running these myself taught me things a job rarely does: how to price something, when to ship versus keep polishing, and what users actually respond to once a product is out in the world.</p>
                         <p data-i18n="about_p3">There's a quieter part of my life too. After major surgery and the birth of my eldest child, I started donating blood regularly, and in 2026 hit my <strong>50th donation</strong>, recognised by NHS Blood and Transplant. It's a small, repeatable way of putting something back.</p>
                         <p data-i18n="about_p4">I also write, though not often and not because I'd call myself a writer. Some thoughts just need somewhere to land. A few of those essays are published on <strong>Medium</strong>, and you can find them in the Writing section below.</p>
